    { "grep", "semantic-query-report", "json", "--json", "before-double-dash", "json", "urn:jash:grep-query:v1", (const char*)JASH_BUILTIN_CONTRACT_TEXT_2, "mixed", "Both encoders consume owned observed records. Source bytes are read completely and checked before that source publishes results. JSON contains items+summary; native contains the same item rows then one summary, with JSC1 open-record schema and exact row semantics validated by the published projection schema and native kind tests. A true quiet/file predicate can be complete without evaluating later lines/sources; scan_complete distinguishes that. False predicate is COMPLETE/status1/errors0 only after needed evaluation. Source failures are FAILED/status2, collection/work limits INCOMPLETE/status75, match/page limits INCOMPLETE with predicate status. Accepted cancel preserves130/143; terminal is authoritative over an earlier summary when a later control/delivery event changes stream outcome. -m0 emits only incomplete summary without reading any source. Logical credits measure canonical JDV1 encoded values, not IO/CPU. Paths are JDV_PATH, content JDV_BYTES, counters U64, status/errno I64. A semantic query is selected by any count/list/invert/quiet/context/fuzzy/smart flag, absent source operands or explicit stdin operand -, or by explicit --offset/--limit in JSON mode. Otherwise the historical exact-match shape is retained. All locally implemented search engines and result modes; excludes full external PCRE semantics and human usage/version controls.", "urn:jash:builtin-error:v1", "bytes", "{\"argv\":256,\"argv_bytes\":65536,\"expanded_short_flags\":480,\"patterns_after_newline_split\":64,\"filter_patterns_per_kind\":16,\"filter_bytes\":127,\"source_bytes\":67108864,\"total_source_bytes\":268435456,\"line_bytes\":65535,\"rows_before_summary\":4096,\"recursive_depth\":64,\"recursive_visits\":100000,\"recursive_path_bytes\":4095,\"since_chain_bytes\":16777216,\"since_chain_records\":65536,\"since_chain_line_bytes\":65536,\"since_timestamp_seconds_max\":9223372036854775807,\"since_source_policy\":\"read-only trusted store, nonblocking regular file, stable descriptor/EOF, malformed rows refused, no attestation verification\",\"semantic_arena_bytes\":25165824,\"summary_reserve_bytes\":524288,\"native_logical_bytes\":33554432,\"physical_stream_bytes\":33554432,\"result_rows\":4096,\"summary_rows\":1,\"context_before_max\":4096,\"context_after_max\":4096,\"fuzzy_pattern_bytes\":64,\"smart_pattern_bytes\":255,\"fuzzy_distance\":2,\"fuzzy_work_matrix_cells\":50000000,\"stdin_poll_milliseconds\":50,\"prose_budget\":\"native bypass; JSON whole-document checked and returns separate output_budget_exceeded on exhaustion\",\"transport_failure_status\":125,\"argument_constraints\":[\"Options recognized before -- even after operands. Short flags can be bundled; option values remain indivisible argv tokens. Unknown or conflicting JSON/native selectors fail explicitly.\",\"A provided -e/--regexp pattern makes all positional operands sources; repeated and newline-separated patterns form a union, preserving independent BRE/ERE/fixed grammar.\",\"Matcher precedence: fuzzy, then smart, then fixed, then PCRE-lite, then ERE, then BRE. -G is accepted compatibility default and does not clear another engine flag.\",\"Heuristic fuzzy/smart engines are always case-insensitive and use their own literal rules; -i/-w/-x do not alter those engines.\",\"Result precedence: quiet > files-without-match > count > files-with-matches > spans or selected lines. Context is emitted only in line/span modes.\",\"Explicit file symlinks are followed and named identity revalidated; recursive symlink entries are skipped. Filters and --since apply to regular files encountered by recursive walk.\",\"Cooperative protocol cancellation is admitted only when the output selector is the first argument. Named FIFO operands are rejected; stdin pipe polling checks control every 50ms.\",\"No external command or human-output capture/reparse participates in these structured variants.\"],\"runtime_cancellation\":true,\"logical_credit\":null,\"presentation_budget\":\"The complete JSON document is encoded and measured with a 32 MiB buffer ceiling, then checked against a positive JASH_LLM_BUDGET (32 MiB when no positive budget is configured). Exhaustion returns a separate output_budget_exceeded or output_limit_exceeded document with status 75; encoding or delivery failure returns 125.\",\"projection_schema_path\":\"schemas/builtin-grep-query-v1.schema.json\"}", "[{\"grammar\":\"[MATCH_OPTIONS] [-c|-l|-L|-v|-q|--fuzzy|--smart|-A N|-B N|-C [N]] [-e PATTERN ... | PATTERN] [FILE|DIR|- ...]\",\"effect\":\"read\"},{\"grammar\":\"[MATCH_OPTIONS] [-e PATTERN ... | PATTERN] (no source operands: read stdin to EOF)\",\"effect\":\"read\"},{\"grammar\":\"[MATCH_OPTIONS] [-e PATTERN ... | PATTERN] FILE|- ... (one or more explicit stdin operands -)\",\"effect\":\"read\"},{\"grammar\":\"[MATCH_OPTIONS] --offset N [--limit N] [-e PATTERN ... | PATTERN] FILE|DIR ... (JSON page report)\",\"effect\":\"read\"}]", "[\"tests/test_grep_semantic_data.py\",\"tests/test_grep_native_data.py\",\"tests/test_grep_gold.sh\",\"tests/test_jinv127_grep_cluster.sh\",\"tests/test_jinv104_grep_include_union.sh\"]", "[\"linux\"]", 1, 1 },
    { "grep", "semantic-query-records", "data", "--data", "before-double-dash", "jtv2", NULL, (const char*)JASH_BUILTIN_CONTRACT_TEXT_3, "typed-terminal", "Both encoders consume owned observed records. Source bytes are read completely and checked before that source publishes results. JSON contains items+summary; native contains the same item rows then one summary, with JSC1 open-record schema and exact row semantics validated by the published projection schema and native kind tests. A true quiet/file predicate can be complete without evaluating later lines/sources; scan_complete distinguishes that. False predicate is COMPLETE/status1/errors0 only after needed evaluation. Source failures are FAILED/status2, collection/work limits INCOMPLETE/status75, match/page limits INCOMPLETE with predicate status. Accepted cancel preserves130/143; terminal is authoritative over an earlier summary when a later control/delivery event changes stream outcome. -m0 emits only incomplete summary without reading any source. Logical credits measure canonical JDV1 encoded values, not IO/CPU. Paths are JDV_PATH, content JDV_BYTES, counters U64, status/errno I64. A semantic query is selected by any count/list/invert/quiet/context/fuzzy/smart flag, absent source operands or explicit stdin operand -, or by explicit --offset/--limit in JSON mode. Otherwise the historical exact-match shape is retained. All locally implemented search engines and result modes; excludes full external PCRE semantics and human usage/version controls.", NULL, "bytes", "{\"argv\":256,\"argv_bytes\":65536,\"expanded_short_flags\":480,\"patterns_after_newline_split\":64,\"filter_patterns_per_kind\":16,\"filter_bytes\":127,\"source_bytes\":67108864,\"total_source_bytes\":268435456,\"line_bytes\":65535,\"rows_before_summary\":4096,\"recursive_depth\":64,\"recursive_visits\":100000,\"recursive_path_bytes\":4095,\"since_chain_bytes\":16777216,\"since_chain_records\":65536,\"since_chain_line_bytes\":65536,\"since_timestamp_se